<title>FRANCE: Algeria earns $2.5 mln from fishing fees in 1996.</title>
<headline>Algeria earns $2.5 mln from fishing fees in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria earned $2.5 million on fees from foreign fishing vessels, mostly Japanese, in 1996, the official Algerian news agency APS said on Monday.</p>
<p>The country expects to reap about $5 million from fees levied on foreign fishers in 1997, said APS quoting an official in the Algerian national fishing company (ENAPECHE).</p>
<p>Algeria opened its territorial waters to foreign vessels for the first time last April.</p>
<p>The government earns 130,000 dinars ($2,321.4) for each tonne fished by a foreign vessel, officials said.</p>
<p>($ = 56 dinars)</p>
